cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository's Lean development, generators, or artifacts in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Lean 4 formalization of boundary-colouring structure and triangle disk-gadget synthesis for the four-colour problem"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lei
    given-names: Yue-Hui
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 + mathlib development studying the boundary-colouring structure of the
  four-colour problem. It provides an exact boundary-colouring relation over
  ordered boundary injections, finite enumeration of C5 boundary states, a gadget
  relation algebra, and a deterministic certificate pipeline that re-checks graph,
  boundary and colouring claims in Lean instead of trusting the Python search.
  The finite-state layer models a fixed triangle grammar twice: ColorDFA carries an
  exact Sigma semantics for every attachment word as ordinary Lean proofs, whereas
  GeometryDFA only claims forward soundness (an accepted word yields a rotation
  system passing an Euler and face checker), its completeness direction remaining
  an explicit topology gap. Results are reported under a stated trust hierarchy
  ("proved in Lean", "computationally observed", "conjectured"). The repository does
  not prove the four-colour theorem, and neither assumes it as an axiom nor uses it
  as a search oracle.
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.1.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/raylei50653/math"
